A. The finance director;
B. The accounting manager;
C. The city manager or the administrative assistant if one has been appointed by the city manager;
D. The mayor;
E. The city clerk; or
F. A member of the city council designated by the city council at its first regular meeting in January of each year to serve until the next year or until a successor is appointed. The name of the person so appointed and authorized to countersign checks issued on the city treasury shall be spread upon the minutes of the first regular meeting of the mayor and council in each calendar year.
